# A ring-0 read of an upper-half address no page table maps (PML4 slot 300)
# is a kernel bug: the #PF handler panics with one report naming the vector,
# the decoded error code, CR2, RIP and RSP (docs/design.md, "Interrupts and
# exceptions taken in ring 0").
cmdline: test=page_fault
exit: failure
expect: microL4 kernel
expect: KERNEL PANIC at kernel/src/arch/x86_64/trap.rs:
expect: fatal trap:
expect: PF page fault (vector 14) in ring 0: error 0x0 (not present, supervisor read), CR2 0xffff960000000000, RIP 0xffffffff8
expect: RSP 0xffffffff8
expect: CS 0x8, frame on the kernel stack
expect: rax
expect: r15
